  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Crisis Analysis: Impact of Cross-Border Trends on Benin and Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mercy Corps will leverage its Crisis Analysis expertise and operational presence in the region, as well as ongoing research for an FCDO-funded program in Benin (BSL) and previous research funded in the area, to propose two types of analytical products. These will aim at providing detailed, inclusive and community-centred comparative perspectives on the existing and expectedconflict resilience, socio-economic dynamics, human security issues, and population movement patterns in the border areas. Additionally, the analytical products will incorporate an innovative visual approach (maps and dashboards) to monitor the triggers and dynamics of events generally associated with herder-farmer conflicts, considered by both governments and other stakeholders as one of the root causes of human insecurity and political grievances, using a combination of technological tools and human-led analysis</narrative>
  </description>
